# Defect 398 across a module (lane b13-unit, 2026-10-06): `helper.bump` named
# as a value is refused where it stands, named as the author wrote it, and the
# qualified call beside it is quiet. No `check/` case holds a second module,
# so `suite_surface`'s row is this shape's golden.
#
# Corrected 2026-11-26, panel 261's R1 (ratified, decision 2827): a function
# of the program is a value of the type its signature writes, marks
# included, across a module too, so `helper.bump` is a value of
# `(function(@i64) -> ())` and a call through it writes the place, as the
# qualified call does: the program prints 3.
use helper

function main()
    f = helper.bump
    x: i64 @= 1
    helper.bump(@x)
    f(@x)
    print(x)
